Let’s build a Min-Heap step by step. The core idea is simple: whenever we insert a value, we place it at the end and then move it *upward* until the heap property is restored.

```js
class MinHeap {
  constructor() {
    this.heap = [];
  }

  insert(value) {
    this.heap.push(value);
    this.bubbleUp();
  }

  bubbleUp() {
    let index = this.heap.length - 1;
    const element = this.heap[index];

    while (index > 0) {
      let parentIndex = Math.floor((index - 1) / 2);
      let parent = this.heap[parentIndex];

      if (element >= parent) break;

      this.heap[parentIndex] = element;
      this.heap[index] = parent;
      index = parentIndex;
    }
  }
}
```

Imagine adding a new book to a pile where the lightest book must always stay on top. You drop the book on top, then keep swapping it downward until the rule is satisfied.

This operation runs in **O(log n)** time because each swap moves one level up the tree.

**Think About This**: Why does bubbling up never need to check all elements in the heap?

Removing the minimum element means removing the root. But removing the root would break the tree, so we replace it with the last element and then push that element *downward* until order is restored.

```js
extractMin() {
  const min = this.heap[0];
  const end = this.heap.pop();

  if (this.heap.length > 0) {
    this.heap[0] = end;
    this.sinkDown();
  }

  return min;
}

sinkDown() {
  let index = 0;
  const length = this.heap.length;
  const element = this.heap[0];

  while (true) {
    let leftIndex = 2 * index + 1;
    let rightIndex = 2 * index + 2;
    let swap = null;

    if (leftIndex < length && this.heap[leftIndex] < element) {
      swap = leftIndex;
    }

    if (
      rightIndex < length &&
      this.heap[rightIndex] < (swap === null ? element : this.heap[leftIndex])
    ) {
      swap = rightIndex;
    }

    if (swap === null) break;

    this.heap[index] = this.heap[swap];
    this.heap[swap] = element;
    index = swap;
  }
}
```

This is like removing the top card from a deck, replacing it with the bottom card, and then shuffling downward until the order feels right again.

