The **two-pointer technique** is used when working with arrays or strings, especially when data is sorted or when searching for pairs.

Mental model: imagine two fingers moving from different ends of a list, shrinking the search space with every move.

```js
function hasPairWithSum(arr, target) {
  let left = 0;
  let right = arr.length - 1;

  while (left < right) {
    const sum = arr[left] + arr[right];
    if (sum === target) return true;
    if (sum < target) left++;
    else right--;
  }
  return false;
}
```

