Sliding window is ideal for problems involving **subarrays or substrings**.

Instead of recalculating from scratch, you reuse previous computation by sliding the window forward.

```js
function maxSubarraySum(arr, k) {
  let maxSum = 0;
  let windowSum = 0;

  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    windowSum += arr[i];
    if (i >= k - 1) {
      maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, windowSum);
      windowSum -= arr[i - k + 1];
    }
  }
  return maxSum;
}
```

