Fast and slow pointers move through data at different speeds.

Mental model: two runners on a track - if there is a loop, the faster one will eventually catch up.

```js
function hasCycle(head) {
  let slow = head;
  let fast = head;

  while (fast && fast.next) {
    slow = slow.next;
    fast = fast.next.next;
    if (slow === fast) return true;
  }
  return false;
}
```

