DFS and BFS are fundamental traversal patterns.

DFS explores deeply before backtracking. BFS explores level by level.

```js
function bfs(graph, start) {
  const queue = [start];
  const visited = new Set([start]);

  while (queue.length) {
    const node = queue.shift();
    for (let next of graph[node]) {
      if (!visited.has(next)) {
        visited.add(next);
        queue.push(next);
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Used in trees, graphs, grids, and shortest-path problems.

