## Extracting Reusable Logic

Let’s build a custom hook that tracks the browser window width. This logic might be useful in many components, such as responsive layouts or conditional rendering.

```jsx
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

function useWindowWidth() {
  const [width, setWidth] = useState(window.innerWidth);

  useEffect(() => {
    const handleResize = () => setWidth(window.innerWidth);
    window.addEventListener('resize', handleResize);

    return () => window.removeEventListener('resize', handleResize);
  }, []);

  return width;
}

export default useWindowWidth;
```

The hook encapsulates state, side effects, and cleanup. Any component using it does not need to know how resize events work.

