  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Failed to save data', error);
  }
};
```

The `async/await` pattern is important here. AsyncStorage operations are asynchronous because they may involve disk access, which is slower than memory. Blocking the UI while saving data would result in a poor user experience.

In real apps, this pattern is commonly used after login, onboarding completion, or when a user updates preferences. For example, after a successful login API call, you might store the authentication token locally so the user does not need to log in again.

