Navigation is rarely just movement. Screens often need data. React Navigation allows parameters to be passed during navigation.

```js
navigation.navigate('Details', { itemId: 42, otherParam: 'Hello' });

function DetailsScreen({ route }) {
  const { itemId, otherParam } = route.params;
  return (
    <View>
      <Text>Item ID: {itemId}</Text>
      <Text>Other Param: {otherParam}</Text>
    </View>
  );
}
```

Think of params as a package delivered along with navigation. They provide context for the destination screen.

