Primitives are the building blocks of data. In TypeScript, you explicitly declare them using keywords.

```typescript
let name: string = "Alice";
let age: number = 30;
let isStudent: boolean = true;
let nothing: null = null;
let undefinedVar: undefined = undefined;
```

**Key Rule:** The type must match the value. If you declare `string`, you can only assign strings.

